Subject: [PATCH] SS-5 v0.2: Light-nuclei binding from open-vertex cascade

Major revision from v0.1 (deuteron-only) to cover light nuclei A=2,3,4.

Central result: zero-parameter cascade formula
  B(A,Z) = (A-1) n_np (M_0/phi) - n_pp (alpha_em hbar c)/(1.2 A^(1/3))
         - (n_pp+n_nn)(M_0/phi^3) + delta_{A,4}(M_0/phi)

Four quantitative predictions within the CPP residual band:
  d    = 2.342 MeV (+5.3%)
  3H   = 8.474 MeV (-0.09%)
  3He  = 7.642 MeV (-1.0%)
  4He  = 27.904 MeV (-1.4%)

Three structural unboundness predictions, all confirmed:
  5He  unbound (S_n = -0.89 MeV)
  5Li  unbound (S_p = -1.97 MeV)
  8Be  near-threshold unbound (-92 keV, triple-alpha bottleneck)

Mechanism (Thomas's 17 April 2026 reframe, v0.1 superseded):
  - Base-to-base nucleon configuration predominant, vertex-to-vertex
    excluded by quantitative fit + cascade extensibility
  - Three qq DP chains across triangular contact face K3-reduced to
    one collective pair quantum B_pair = M_0/phi = 2.342 MeV
  - Cascade factor (A-1) from closed-polytope completion counting
  - Pauli penalty M_0/phi^3 per like-pair (propagation-step argument)
  - Closure bonus M_0/phi at A=4 (tetrahedral polytope)

Epistemic status:
  - Two load-bearing coefficients (A-1) and M_0/phi^3 are motivated
    but not rigorously derived; flagged as CONJ-SS-11 and registered
    OPEN-SS-19 for future derivation.
  - K3 collective-mode reduction at base contact is Conjecture 2.4.
  - Heavy-nuclei alpha-cluster regime (A>=6) registered as OPEN-SS-18.

