+
+## PHEN-V — Consilience with CPP programme
+
+Pair binding $M_0/\varphi = m_e z/\varphi^2$ and Pauli coefficient $M_0/\varphi^3$ use only constants that appear elsewhere in the programme:
+
+- $M_0$: DP energy quantum (SM-8, SM-9, SM-10)
+- $\eta = 1/\varphi$: propagation efficiency (SM-6, SM-7, SM-8, SS-4)
+- K$_3$ spectrum $\{+2, -1, -1\}$: same as Koide face (SM-3), Gell-Mann mode basis (SS-3), quark mass structure (SM-6, SM-7)
+- Closed-polytope cascade: generalises SS-1/SS-3 internal-cage mode counting to inter-nucleon polytopes
+
+SS-5 v0.2 is *structurally consistent* with every earlier CPP paper — it applies existing rules to a new sector.
+
+---
+
+## Falsification routes
+
+**Quantitative:** Any of the four A=2,3,4 bindings predicted outside the CPP residual band ($\sim \pm 5\%$) would falsify. Currently all four are within the band.
+
+**$(A-1)$ multiplicity:** Alternative factors $(A-1)^2$ or $(A-1)/2$ give $^3$H/$^3$He predictions outside the band. The data select $(A-1)$.
+
+**Pauli coefficient:** Alternative coefficients $M_0/\varphi^2$ (1.45 MeV) or $M_0/\varphi^4$ (0.55 MeV) give $^3$H, $^3$He, $^4$He predictions outside the band. The data select $M_0/\varphi^3 = 0.895$ MeV.
+
+**Closure bonus:** Removing the A=4 bonus would push $^4$He to 25.55 MeV (−9.7% error, outside band). The data confirm the closure bonus.
+
+**Unboundness predictions:** Discovery of bound $^5$He, $^5$Li, or $^8$Be would falsify the closed-polytope-gap argument. No such observation in 70+ years of nuclear physics.
+
+---
+
+## Independence from prior CPP results
+
+SS-5 v0.2 does not rest on:
+- Operator formalism (Layer B of SM-3, SS-3): K$_3$ reduction is structural, not operator-algebraic.
+- Gibbs equilibration (SM-3): no thermal assumption.
+- Koide algebra (SM-6): this is nuclear-sector, not lepton-mass.
+- String tension σ (SS-4): the cascade pairs carry collective K$_3$ mode, not confining flux tube.
+
+This is a genuinely orthogonal star shot under the swarm-validation doctrine. Nothing in the nuclear sector is inherited from the Koide/cage-mass thread.
